usage: chat [options] serve | replay SCRIPT | load | drill

serve    serve clients until Ctrl-C or SHUTDOWN
replay   run SCRIPT's clients against an in-process server and print the transcript
load     connect many clients at once and print what they saw
drill    cancel the server at each of its waits and report how each ended

Options:
  --help                 Show this help
  --addr <str>           Address to listen on (serve: 127.0.0.1:7070; others: a free loopback port)
  --motd <str>           File whose first line is the message of the day
  --history <str>        File to write every room message to
  --max-clients <int>    Connections served at once (default 64, at most 1024)
  --queue <int>          Room messages queued per client before it is dropped as too slow (default 64)
  --burst <int>          Messages a client may send between refills, 0 for no limit (default 20)
  --refill-ms <int>      Milliseconds between rate refills (default 1000)
  --client-memory <int>  Bytes each connection may use for its own state (default 4096)
  --token <str>          Operator token for OPER and SHUTDOWN (default: none)
  --bots <int>           Bots to start, 0 to 2 (default 2)
  --clients <int>        load: clients to connect (default 100)
  --rooms <int>          load: rooms to spread them over (default 10)
  --messages <int>       load: messages each client sends (default 5)
  --shutdown             load: end by shutting the server down under every client
  --slow                 load: one client that never reads, and one that floods its room
  --deadline <int>       replay and load: seconds before giving up and reporting what was seen, 0 for never (default 20)
  --idle-ms <int>        Milliseconds a connection may sit with nothing read or sent before it is dropped, 0 for never (default 0)
  --record               Log every byte each TCP connection reads and writes (implies --log info)
  --log <str>            Log level on stderr: debug, info, warn or error (default warn)
  --web <str>            Also serve the web front end (WebSocket and event streams) on this address
  --web-tls-chain <str>  PEM certificate chain for the HTTPS web front end
  --web-tls-key <str>    PEM private key for the HTTPS web front end
  --web-cacert <str>     PEM roots to trust when replay connects to the HTTPS web front end
Arguments:
  <args>...              The command and its file
